;;; REGION CLAIM — R empty, and the alive node that owes. M1e2 S1e2.1a.4.
;;;
;;; Ann likes neither food and every person owes a liking, so root owes, and
;;; cannot pay: the obligation proposes Ann's two likings and each is stored as
;;; false. Nothing is left to guess, so root is the only node: R is empty of
;;; the second kind, and the one alive, owing node with no alive node above it
;;; is root itself. Its `likes` extent is what `(owing …)` states; under R a
;;; claim that listed it as a state of R would be false. The program is
;;; tests/stdlib/algebra/23_total_owed.ein's with Ann's two negatives.
;;;
;;; Until M1f S1f.6.34 it had no negatives and wrote `:no-hypothesis (is-a
;;; likes)`, keeping the obligation from proposing what it owes; a list may
;;; not filter what an obligation owes since (*"filtered obligations are
;;; nonsense by definition"*, the user, 2026-11-13), and the debt is made
;;; unpayable by the program's own facts instead. R and the claim did not move.

(import std.algebra :symbols (total-owed))
(relation is-a  T T :why "{?1} is a {?2}")
(relation likes Person Food :why "{?1} likes {?2}")
(is-a Ann Person) (is-a Bob Person)
(is-a Soup Food)  (is-a Stew Food)
(total-owed likes is-a)
(likes Bob Stew)
(not (likes Ann Soup)) (not (likes Ann Stew))

(solve
  :no-hypothesis (is-a)
  :expect (region
            (owing (model (likes Bob Stew)))))

(query :goal (likes ?who ?what))
